{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender UI Block.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender UI Block.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender ui block blender ui block","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender UI Block.md","fileName":"Blender UI Block.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender UI Block","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Editor Construction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Editor Construction","Blender UI Button","Blender Editor Button Operator Binding","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender UI Block.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender UI Block.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender ui block blender ui block","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender UI Block.md","fileName":"Blender UI Block.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender UI Block","heading":"Blender UI Block","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A Blender UI block groups related interface controls within a region. Button-definition functions receive the block so layout, interaction, and selection behavior can be coordinated among controls rather than treating every widget as an isolated drawing command.\n\nThe custom editor's header draw callback passes a block while creating each [[Blender UI Button]]. Groups can support relationships such as radial or mutually exclusive choices, and [[Blender Editor Button Operator Binding]] attaches application behavior after the control is defined.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Editor Construction","Blender UI Button","Blender Editor Button Operator Binding","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender UI Block.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blende